      equipment: 'Domino set and score tracker (chips or score sheet).',
      dealing: 'Each player receives 7 tiles; all tiles are dealt, so there is no boneyard.',
    },
    turnFlow: 'Lead is by lot in the first hand and then rotates. Opening lead must be a double or a scoring starter tile such as 0-5, 1-4, 2-3, 4-6, or 5-5; if unavailable, lead passes onward. Players match open ends or pass if blocked. Any scoring play or any double gives an immediate extra turn. If a player uses their last tile on a scoring play or double, they are washed up and play continues among others. A hand ends when a player dominoes on a non-scoring non-double play, or when the game blocks.',
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'All Fives dominoes scores by multiples of five; no ante.',
      deal: 'System/dealer action at hand start.',
      reveal_market: 'No market exists in Seven-Toed Pete.',
      buy_market: 'No market purchases exist in Seven-Toed Pete.',
      buy_stock: 'No stock buying exists in standard four-player Seven-Toed Pete.',
      fold: 'No folding in Seven-Toed Pete; a player either plays a legal tile or passes.',
      check: 'No betting; score by making end-totals multiples of five.',
      call: 'Tile-matching game; no call or betting. Muggins is optional score claim.',
      bet: 'Scoring is by end-sums and hand bonus; no betting.',
      raise: 'No betting in All Fives dominoes.',
      declare: 'No declaration phase; play tiles to layout ends, score on multiples of 5.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hand is played out tile by tile; no formal reveal. Blocked hand scores by pips.',
      award_pot: 'System action at hand end.',
      play_card: 'Tile must match an open end; first double played is the only spinner.',
      draw: 'All tiles are dealt in the standard four-player form; no boneyard draw.',
      discard: 'Tiles are placed on layout ends; no discard pile. Draw when blocked.',
      pass: 'Only legal when no matching play exists.',
      bid: 'No bidding; any tile may be led. Score by matching ends and multiples of 5.',
      meld: 'Domino placement game; no melds. Tiles match open ends only.',
      go_out: 'Hand ends when a player dominoes (plays last tile) or game is blocked.',
    },
    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 7 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Outscore opponents by making scoring plays and winning hands through domino or lowest blocked-hand pip total.',
      'Turn-flow example: Lead is by lot in the first hand and then rotates. Opening lead must be a double or a scoring starter tile such as 0-5, 1-4, 2-3, 4-6, or 5-5; if unavailable, lead passes onward. Players match open ends or pass if blocked. Any scoring play or any double gives an immediate extra turn. If a player uses their last tile on a scoring play or double, they are washed up and play continues among others. A hand ends when a player dominoes on a non-scoring non-double play, or when the game blocks.',
      "Scoring example: Score when exposed ends total a multiple of five. Hand winner (domino or blocked-hand low pip total) also scores opponents' remaining pips, commonly converted by dividing by five after rounding. Reach the table-agreed target score before opponents..",
